# ReproPerturb Data Analysis Repository

Welcome to the code repository associated with our manuscript. This folder provides an organized entry point for the scripts used in the downstream processing, visualization, quality assessment, and figure-related analyses described in our study.

> **⚠️ Important Notice Regarding the ReproPerturb Model**
> At this stage, the repository does **not** include the full ReproPerturb model implementation, training pipeline, model checkpoints, or internal large-scale screening scripts. 
>
> *The ReproPerturb-related core codebase will be updated and released upon manuscript acceptance, in strict accordance with our final software release plan and applicable intellectual-property requirements (Patent Application: CN 202610444456.X).*

---

## 🗂️ Current Scope and Content Status

| Content Type | Status | Description |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Data analysis scripts** | ✅ *Included / Organizing* | Scripts related to processing, summary analysis, visualization, and figure generation. |
| **Utility scripts** | ✅ *Included where relevant* | Helper functions and subroutines used by the analysis workflow. |
| **ReproPerturb model code** | ⏳ *Pending acceptance* | The model architecture, training workflow, and inference code. |
| **Model checkpoints** | ⏳ *Pending acceptance* | Pre-trained weights; availability will follow the final release policy. |
| **Large-scale screening scripts** | ⏳ *Pending acceptance* | ReproPerturb screening code will be provided later where appropriate. |

---

## 📌 Notes for Users

* **Analysis-Oriented:** The code currently available in this directory should be interpreted as analysis-oriented material to support reproducibility, rather than a fully packaged, standalone software suite. 
* **Evolving Documentation:** File organization and documentation may continue to evolve as the manuscript proceeds through peer review and publication.
* **Methodological Details:** For ReproPerturb-specific implementation details, please refer to the *Materials and Methods* and *Supplementary Information* sections of our manuscript. 
* **Future Updates:** Additional code, comprehensive usage examples, and detailed release notes will be systematically added to this repository following the formal acceptance of the paper
